{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And fifty loops.</b> The place of the fifty loops holds three and a half cubits. How so? When you give half a cubit for each gap of the forty-nine gaps that are in them, they amount to twenty-four and a half cubits, and there remain for you three and a half cubits for the place of the clasps, to complete up to twenty-eight cubits, which is the length of the curtain. But the goat-hair curtains, which held thirty cubits in length — subtract from them twenty-four and a half cubits for the forty-nine gaps, and there remain for you five and a half cubits for the place of these loops, because they are thicker and coarser than the others." "<b>Opposite the loops.</b> Rashi interpreted, and the verse supports me, as it is written: 'and you shall place the curtain under the clasps.' And if according to the words of this baraita, the curtain would be drawn one cubit away from the clasps. Some reconcile the baraita with the verse and say that the pillars of the curtain are set exactly at the twenty-cubit mark, and the curtain is suspended and spread on them from there outward toward the east — so the curtain is indeed placed under the clasps. And according to the words of tractate Shabbat: if the pillars are exactly at the twenty, the curtain is suspended on them from there inward toward the west; and if they are exactly at the twenty-one, the curtain is suspended on them from there outward toward the east."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:36.530236053Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}